# 📦 SupplySense Project Map

A comprehensive guide to the folders and files in the SupplySense warehouse management system.

## 📂 Root Directory
- `client/`: The React-based frontend application.
- `server/`: The Node.js/Express backend API.
- `ml/`: Machine Learning module for demand forecasting.
- `docs/`: Architecture and design documentation.
- `docker-compose.yml`: Infrastructure configuration for Docker deployment.
- `package.json`: Root-level dependencies and script definitions.

---

## 💻 📁 client/ (Frontend)
Built with React and Vite.
- `src/main.jsx`: Entry point that mounts the React application.
- `src/App.jsx`: The core of the frontend. Contains:
    - `Gate`: Authentication and role selection (Customer/Manager).
    - `CustomerPortal`: Shopping experience, compact filtering, and QR checkout.
    - `Manager`: Operations dashboard, inventory tracking, and supplier approval.
- `src/styles.css`: Global theme, localized Indian styling, and layout definitions.

---

## ⚙️ 📁 server/ (Backend)
Built with Node.js, Express, and Prisma ORM.

### 📄 server/prisma/ (Database)
- `schema.prisma`: The single source of truth for the DB schema (Users, Inventory, Orders, Suppliers).
- `seed.js`: Script to populate the DB with 5 Indian warehouses and demo users.
- `migrations/`: Version-controlled SQL changes to the database.

### 📄 server/src/ (Application Logic)
- `server.js`: Server startup, port configuration, and graceful shutdown.
- `app.js`: Express app setup, global middleware (CORS, Helmet), and route registration.

#### 📁 src/routes/ (API Endpoints)
Maps URLs to service logic.
- `auth.routes.js`: Login, registration, and logout.
- `commerce.routes.js`: Cart and Wishlist management.
- `order.routes.js`: Order creation and history.
- `payment.routes.js`: QR scan processing and payment capture.
- `supply.routes.js`: Supplier management and PO approvals.
- `warehouse.routes.js`: Inventory lookups and warehouse details.
- `intelligence.routes.js`: Demand prediction triggers.
- `dashboard.routes.js`: Aggregated data for Manager metrics.

#### 📁 src/services/ (Business Logic)
Where the "brain" of the application lives.
- `supply.service.js`: Handles the Supplier $\rightarrow$ Warehouse loop (PO approvals, Goods Receipts).
- `order.service.js`: Handles the Order $\rightarrow$ Inventory loop (Reservations, Stock locking).
- `payment.service.js`: Handles the Payment $\rightarrow$ Stock subtraction loop.
- `intelligence.service.js`: Manages demand forecasting logic.
- `formula.service.js`: Deterministic math for reorder points.
- `audit.service.js`: Logs every inventory move for traceability.
- `user.service.js`: User profile and role management.

#### 📁 src/middleware/ (Request Pipeline)
- `auth.js`: JWT verification and Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).
- `validate.js`: Zod-based request body validation.
- `error-handler.js`: Global catch-all for `AppError` to send clean API responses.

#### 📁 src/utils/ (Helpers)
- `money.js`: Localized currency formatting for Rupees (₹).
- `app-error.js`: Standardized error class for the entire API.
- `response.js`: Helpers for consistent API response formats.

---

## 🤖 📁 ml/ (Machine Learning)
Dedicated module for demand forecasting.
- `train_demand_model.py`: Python script to train the RandomForest model using M5 data.
- `demand_prediction_model.py`: A clean version of the training logic.
- `demand_prediction_notebook.txt`: Step-by-step guide for Jupyter Notebook implementation.
- `README.md`: Instructions for dataset placement and training.
- `sales_dataset/`: Store for M5 CSV files (`calendar.csv`, etc.).
- `artifacts/`: Stores the output of training (`demand_model.joblib`).
